On Sat, 05 Aug 2006 03:19:10 -0700, corvine@gmail.com wrote:

[the story of Jayne the monk so far]

> Jayne the Student of Stones     St:18/20 Dx:17 Co:17 In:10 Wi:13 Ch:9
> Neutral
> Dlvl:27 $:2158 HP:108(108) Pw:48(71) AC:-4 Exp:13

>  a - an uncursed +3 pair of leather gloves (being worn)
>  b - an uncursed +1 robe (being worn)
>  m - a rusty +0 helmet (being worn)

Chuck this for an elven leather helm if you're willing to risk the
occasional falling rock, or for a helm of brilliance if you can find one;
it'll give you another AC point and improve those spell failure rates.

>  u - an uncursed +0 pair of elven boots (being worn)

OK, that's four points for the gloves, three for the robe, none for the
helmet and one for the boots.  So you have six points divine protection. 
You can get three more before it starts to become a crapshoot.

> I don't have levitation/water walking and my wand of cold is empty. I
> think I need to go back up into the dungeons and improve my AC somehow
> (maybe explore a couple of levels more fully and try and find an altar)

Are those six points from prayer?  You can get them from the Minetown
priest.  It doesn't matter if he's cross-aligned.  400 times your level in
gold will do it.  You're at level 13, so 15600 zorkmids will get you those
three points.

Can you find Fort Ludios?  Wipe out the soldiers, altarize whatever armor
looks good, you might improve upon those boots.  And get those 15600
zorkmids.  Of course you'll probably want a bag of some sort for
mass-altarizing of armor.

As for taking on the Castle:  it seems you weren't set upon by purple Ls
upon arrival.  Not a bad start.  Remember your basic combat techniques. 
The Eye will keep you safe from any golden nagas.  Watch out for those
eels.

And don't linger on the drawbridge.  One soldier shows up with a wand of
striking and you will be toast.  You might try blowing the drawbridge
yourself, and then toasting the enemy with magic missiles from across the
moat.

